    "section_text": "Computer Science Minor Curriculum A student with a minor in computer science must meet the following requirements: A \"C\" or better grade in the following core courses: COMP SCI 1500 Computational Problem Solving (Note that COMP SCI 1500 will be waived in lieu of a score of 4 or 5 on the AP Computer Science A exam and no additional credit hours will be required.) 3 COMP SCI 1570 Introduction To C++ Programming 3 COMP SCI 1575 Data Structures 3 COMP SCI 1580 Introduction To Programming Laboratory 1 COMP SCI 1585 Data Structures Laboratory 1 A \"C\" or better grade in at least 9 credit hours of COMP SCI courses in addition to the above listed core courses, excluding: COMP SCI 2001 - Domain Exploration and Innovation Methods COMP SCI 3001 - Skill Development for Entrepreneurs and Innovators COMP SCI 4001 - Advanced Domain Exploration and Innovation Methods COMP SCI 4001 - Interpersonal Dynamics for Entrepreneurs and Innovators COMP SCI 4700 Intellectual Property For Computer Scientists 3 All COMP SCI x9xx courses At most 6 credit hours can be transfer credits and transfer classes must show a \"C\" or better grade.",
